content:
@jodiecongirl GLP-1= Semaglutide (Ozempic &amp; Wegovy): reduces appetite, slows digestion. 

Dual agonist GLP-1 + GIP= Tirzepatide (Mounjaro &amp; Zepbound): as above + lowers blood sugar, manages fat deposition (burning more fat).

So neither of them just work on appetite.

@muscleforlife Me 3 years ago: Trainer. Dietician. Followed everything for 6 months tracking every lick &amp; sniff of food. Lost 10lbs.

Added: Endocrinologist. started me on Wegovy, I continued the same training/diet. Weight started falling off. 

Now you understand what people are paying for 🙄

@FamilyFeud 

Why do these women sorry but most of them are African-American women are so big like fat while there’s so many things now that can help you lose weight I took Wegovy I lost 30 pounds in six months 
What’s the problem with these people

@sweetcarolinatv ... around 15% in studies.
Ozempic (Semaglutide): The same active ingredient as Wegovy (semaglutide) but FDA-approved for Type 2 Diabetes; often used off-label for weight loss.
Saxenda (Liraglutide): A daily injection used to manage weight by controlling appetite

@JonahLupton The gelatine acts as a Satiety effect to make you feel full as glp-1 would.
I tried the Wegovy 4 MG dosages for 3 weeks and quit from the Nauseous / sick feeling

I know from my experience!!!! Jonah, you would not take either pill or shot, so I dont believe in them! Lost 8 pounds

@drmarlonperalta Gained 22 lbs. on Semaglutide.  Hungry all the time.

Lost 170 lbs. on Tirzepatide.  Hunger is manageable.

Cannot stand even the smell of food with Retatrutide.  Eating is a chore.
